  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is hanging from a spring of force constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The mass is pulled slightly downward and released so that it executes free simple harmonic motion with time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The time when the kinetic energy and potential energy of the system will&nbsp;become equal, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is ________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>E</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
